WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.380
SPEAKER: How do ideas become industries?

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.690
How do inventions become innovations?

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.320
How do you break through?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.830
In this course on problem-solving
and new venture creation,

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.120
you'll learn how entrepreneurs match
promising technologies with customer

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.690
needs to build successful businesses.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.820
You'll acquire new
analytical skills as you

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.420
navigate the complexities of
the commercialization process,

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.380
moving a technology
from lab to the market.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.810
How will a technology be used?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.180
Is that technology ready?

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.880
How will funding be secured?

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.630
What is the business model?

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:55.350
Throughout this journey, you'll hear
from a variety of experts, including

00:00:55.350 --> 00:01:00.150
founders, funders, and industry
mentors, who will share their advice

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:04.440
and experiences related to
bringing new ideas to market.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.880
Many ideas never move beyond
the lab, and those that do often

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.850
fail to achieve commercial viability.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.430
How do we successfully
match seeds with needs?

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.900
Join us as we unlock the potential
of promising technologies

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.440
and their ability to solve some of
our planet's most urgent challenges.

